title A witness builds what it runs -- Scribe, Vault and Basin stop trusting a comment
prompt The SILENCE seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves; pick up the running thread and take the next infrastructure lap.
think ListAgents at open: no reachable agents. No peer to name, so no file move needed a word. git fetch xy read 0/0 against HEAD cea889a8e1 -- the card I read is the tree I stand on.
think Rota N=3715 by git rev-list --count HEAD, row 0 -- aether, Jupiter, why the work exists, the row that HEARS. Read the threshold, follow-our-compass, the Lindy effect, the grain and the crossing. Two of its sentences chose this lap: "a doc that only ever claims what a green witness shows cannot rot into a lie as the code moves beneath it", and the grain strand "a guard that cannot red guards nothing". A header comment saying "Build first" is a claim no witness keeps.
think Cold roster before touching anything: 91 guards, 85 green, 6 red, tree_at_open=8f317c3e1b74, tree_moved=no. Four reds were the known standing set -- rule_twin 39/36 (custody gate %7), dated_path over its ratchet, and two Pond guards that red on a macOS bench. Two were new and shared one root.
think THE NEW PAIR, and its root. nib_honesty and remember_git_nib both refused on construction/ITINERARY.md's Git nib field: hash 3561104a7f resolves=NO, reach=none, gone=1. `git cat-file -t 3561104a7f` answers "Not a valid object name". The prior lap's own log records the cause in its erratum -- it wrote the nib, then rebased, and a rebase rewrites every hash after the point it replays from. The card was left advertising a commit this repository does not contain. This is the seam REDS %103 named: a commit cannot contain its own hash, so the nib is written in the same breath as the commit, and anything that rewrites that commit orphans it.
think Reds first said close what is agent-closable. Of the four standing reds, rule_twin is Keaton's by name, the Pond pair is a host fact, and dated_path belongs to the folding hand. The nib pair is mine, and it closes by naming this round's own commit rather than by editing prose.
think For the constructive half I took REDS %334 -- a witness builds what it runs, or it proves nothing on a clone -- because it was born in Comlink, which is my lane, and because its ratchet sat exactly at its ceiling: unbuilt_pairs=19 ceiling=19, nothing left to absorb another one.
think Read all nineteen unbuilt pairs and took only the infrastructure services in my half: Scribe's reader (invoked by two witnesses) and dashboard, Vault's shard, Basin's basin. Left alone by lane -- five pond/bin/drawn-terminal pairs (Hush), settlement's two (Dream holds the constellation table), five glow/bin gate pairs (Sound's language custody, and %311 already says so), kumara/bin/contact (Dream worked Kumara this morning), and the astrology room (a closed stack).
think The repair is the shape tools/co/comlink_topology_witness.rish already carried and %334 landed in two more: keep the header's "Build first" line, then actually build. Each witness gained `let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"`, a `run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p <room>/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build <module>.rye -femit-bin=<room>/bin/<artifact>"]`, and `assert build.ok else "<name>: build failed -- ${build.err}"` above the first invocation.
think Both witnesses that run scribe/bin/reader build it, rather than one building for the other. Each header tells a reader to run that witness directly, so each keeps its own promise; a build kept by a sibling is real and is still not the promise the file makes.
obs THREE OF THE FOUR TARGET BINARIES WERE ABSENT ON THIS BENCH BEFORE THE LAP. scribe/bin/reader, scribe/bin/dashboard and vault/bin/shard were all missing; only basin/bin/basin survived from some earlier lap. So four of the five witnesses would have died here today, on a working pier, not merely on a hypothetical clone. The scan reports absent_now precisely because it is a fact about one machine, and this machine was already past the point where the comment held.
obs PROVEN FROM BOTH SIDES, on metal, with the binaries deleted first. Repaired, from a clone-like state: all five exit 0 and print their GREEN line, each having built its own artifact. Unrepaired, same state: `git show HEAD:tools/s/scribe_reader_witness.rish` run against an absent binary exits 1 with `rishi: line 13: CommandFailed` naming the run and no cause -- the bare refusal a reader cannot act on, which is the fault this tree already names. A repair proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass.
obs THE METER MOVED, and every number is the scan's own. unbuilt_pairs 19 -> 14, unbuilt_witnesses 18 -> 13, self_built 49 -> 54, absent_now 10 -> 7, built_elsewhere 3 -> 2, invoked_ignored unchanged at 68 over 1,736 witnesses. The ceiling fell to 14 in the three places that spell it: CEILING=14 in the scan, the witness assert `unbuilt_pairs=14 `, and the control's two plants, whose own comment says they track the LIVE ceiling -- so the loop bound moved 19 -> 14 and the one-over plant moved thing20 -> thing15.
obs THE CONTROL PROVES THE NEW CEILING FROM BOTH SIDES rather than inheriting the old one's word: ratchet_counted=yes at 14, ratchet_under_free=yes, ratchet_over_counted=yes at 15, ratchet_over_refused=yes with verdict=witness_without_build. All 21 behaviors read yes, control_verdict=ok, and the witness closes GREEN -- six refusals bitten, fifteen honest readings left free.
obs WHAT THIS LAP DID NOT REACH, named rather than implied. Fourteen pairs still stand, and each of them belongs to a body that is not me. The witness header now says so by name, so the next hand reads which four rooms came home and which are still owed.
obs Declined to book a new REDS row for the orphaned nib, and the reason is two-sided. The pin is full -- 24,571 of 24,576 with zero foldable rows, which is %338 and Keaton's seat -- and the lesson is already written: %103 owns the seam, and the two guards that caught it were built for exactly this and worked. A row that teaches nothing new, written into a pin that cannot hold it, would spend the last bytes on a repeat.
obs QA on touch: six witness headers graded at meter with Service judged rather than assumed -- named_by_card=no, reached (1 to 5 living citers), current, and carried on both sides, so 75 rather than the 100 my first run handed it. Every card reads composite 94, letter A, truth_gate=no. No frame pushed.
obs The card's roster line reads "90 guards, 89 green" and my cold run read 91 and 85. I left it. That line describes the pier, where the two Pond guards pass; overwriting it with a macOS bench's reading would trade one true sentence for another host's, and the card had 30 bytes to spend.
obs THE HOT ROSTER EARNED ITS NAME, and this is the half I did not expect. Cold read geode_libraries green; hot, over the staged tree, read it RED -- docs-geode/libraries/README.md had drifted inside the very commit that staled it. The mechanism is exact: that page counts a witness into a room when the witness REFERENCES the room, and my build lines added the token rye/bin/rye to five files. Two of them, scribe_reader and vault_shard, carried no rye/ reference at all before -- their headers said a bare "rye build" -- so the rye/ row moved 1262 to 1264, and 0 -> 1 for each of those two is the whole of the difference.
obs THE GAP THAT LET IT THROUGH, named rather than booked. tools/hooks/pre-commit rule one fires when a tools/*_witness.rish or a *.rye file ARRIVES or LEAVES. Mine only changed CONTENT, so the hook would not have fired, and the page would have shipped stale to red on somebody else's cold start tomorrow -- REDS %151 and %152 three times over, through a door the trigger does not watch. Regenerated by hand with tools/g/geode_libraries.rish write, staged, and tools/g/geode_libraries_witness.rish re-read GREEN. A row for the trigger gap wants the pin capacity %338 is holding; it is surfaced here and in the recommend rather than smuggled into a full ledger.
obs Hot close: 91 guards, 86 green, 5 red, tree_moved=no, tree_at_close=6f57d3008002. The five were the two nib guards gone green, geode caught and repaired, and the four standing: rule_twin (gate %7), dated_path over its ratchet, and two Pond guards that red on a macOS bench.
